available, that were not part of the defendant’s initial disclosures:
(i) Complaint reports;
(ii) Use of Force reports;
(iii) Defendant officer’s notes, memobook entries, or daily activity 
reports;
(iv) 911 reports, including any recordings;
(v) Radio run reports (audio and written); 
(vi) Any video or photographs of the incident;
(vii) Injury reports;
(viii) Property vouchers;
(ix) Evidence vouchers;
(x) Arrest reports;
(xi) Mugshots;
(xii) Reports of medical treatment for plaintiff while in custody;
(xiii) Desk Appearance Tickets (for arrests after January 2009) or other 
tickets;
(xiv) Summonses; and
(xv) Handwritten Online Booking System forms.
(B) Any documents received from a district attorney’s office or a court 
regarding the incident that forms the basis of the complaint. 
